Patchsu patch 6 (optional, standalone): PP simulation.

Applies on its own to plain osu!lazer (commit 8cb6e6e68d), and also together with every other patch.

A results-screen panel (same layout as the expanded score panel) where every number can be typed into, to see
what a play would be worth. osu! ruleset only.

  Open it from:  song select → Options (F3 / footer button) → "Simulate PP": the selected difficulty with the
                 selected mods, starting at SS.
                 a leaderboard score → right-click → "Simulate PP": starts from that score (its mods, judgements,
                 combo, slider ticks and ends).
                 the results screen of a play → calculator button in the bottom row (next to collection /
                 favourite): starts from the shown score. The panel takes over the one on screen: it starts
                 exactly where the results panel was, with every number already shown (no entrance animation),
                 and only slides into place. The results screen hides while the simulation is open.

  Looks:         the numbers are the results screen's own rolling counters (same font, "98.76%" accuracy format,
                 "/max" suffixes, PERFECT text, staggered entrance, PP dimmed with the tooltip on unranked maps/mods).
                 Clicking a number (or Tab) swaps in a text box until you leave it; the counter then rolls to the value.

  Editable:      accuracy, max combo, PP, 300 / 100 / 50 / miss, slider ticks, slider ends.
                 Spinner spin / bonus are shown but not editable. Total score is recalculated (an estimate once
                 anything changed), rank and the accuracy circle follow.

Rules (everything updates on every keystroke):
- 300 / 100 / 50 / miss always add up to the object count; changing one moves the difference to or from the 300s
  (raising 300s takes from 100s, then 50s, then misses). Accuracy follows at once.
- Judgements never change combo, slider ticks or slider ends. Each miss lowers the highest possible combo by 1,
  each missed slider tick by 2, each missed slider end by 1. A combo that was at the limit follows it (also back up);
  a lower combo stays. A typed combo above the limit is clamped right away. Exception: once an edit leaves no misses
  and no missed slider ticks, the combo jumps to the limit (max combo minus dropped slider ends), so fixing a choke
  is a single edit (setting misses to 0).
- Typing accuracy or PP keeps misses, ticks, ends and combo and turns 300s into 100s (then, if 100s alone can't go
  low enough, 100s into 50s) until the value is as close as it can get. The typed text stays while you type; the box
  shows the real value once you leave it (Enter / click away / Tab). Tab and Shift+Tab move between boxes;
  Tab with nothing selected starts at accuracy (Shift+Tab at the last box).

Footer: the song select footer stays. Back and Mods stay in place, Random / Options slide down (and come back up
on return). Mods opens the normal mod select, but for the simulation only (song select's mods are untouched); a mod
change recalculates the simulation in place (the panel stays, the changed numbers like PP / score / stars roll)
and keeps the typed judgements / ticks / ends / combo. On the right: "Reset to
score" (only when opened from a score; also restores its mods), "Fix choke" (left click: misses become 100s, right
click: misses become 300s; every slider tick is hit and the combo goes to its limit; 100s / 50s and slider ends
stay), "Reset to SS" (keeps the mods), and the hint
"Tab moves to the next one" in the corner.

How it works (for later patches):
- osu.Game/Screens/Ranking/Simulation: PerformanceSimulation (the rules and calculations, no UI),
  PerformanceSimulationScreen (+ its static copy of the expanded ScorePanel), SimulationPanelMiddleContent
  (copy of ExpandedPanelMiddleContent with EditableStatistic boxes), EditableStatistic / SimulationNumberBox.
- PP: the ruleset's PerformanceCalculator with BeatmapDifficultyCache attributes (no pause penalty from 0004).
  A stable score keeps its LegacyTotalScore (used for slider-break guessing) only while nothing was changed.
- Total score: lazer's standardised formula with the combo part estimated from max combo and combo breaks,
  calibrated against the real score when starting from one.
- Footer: new IKeepsSharedFooterButtons marker. ScreenStackFooter forces the vertical transition when entering or
  leaving such a screen, and ScreenFooter.SetButtons(…, keepMatchingLeftButtons) swaps leading left buttons of the
  same type in place without animating (ScreenFooter.SuspendButtons blocks the old ones while the screen loads).
- Entry points are small hunks in FooterButtonOptions.Popover.cs (after the forwarded actions loop),
  BeatmapLeaderboardScore.cs (after "Copy link", before the replay-only items) and ResultsScreen.cs (after the
  favourite button; SimulatePerformanceButton), placed away from 0002/0003's hunks.


